{
 "id": "turbo-html2pdf#29",
 "reason": "HTML documents are styled as Chrome does: <head> <style> sheets apply (all <style> elements in document order), <html>/<body> are real boxes with Chrome's UA rules (body{margin:8px}, head{display:none}, root margins never collapse), rem resolves against the root font size, <style>/<script>/<noscript> text is never painted (html2pdf render path), and the root/body background colour fills the canvas (raster: the propagated colour instead of the first-full-width-box guess; PDF: Page::canvas over the page area). Nearly every output moves by body's 8px margin. Verified Chrome-ward: over the pinned conformance fixtures (fonts pinned to Inter, no margin reset) napi layoutBoxes matches Chrome 156 getBoundingClientRect for 172/209 tagged boxes (base: 1/209), no fixture worse. P5b-Y (turbo-dom consol/p5b-y-layout; turbo-html2pdf consol/p5b-y-layout).",
